# Managed by Ansible (roles/hardening).
# OpenSSH >= 9.8 only. Applied conditionally because older sshd fails to parse it.
#
# The built-in penalty box: sshd tracks per-source-address behaviour and refuses
# connections from addresses that keep failing. This is the kernel-independent
# complement to the nftables meter and fail2ban - it reacts to authentication
# outcomes, which a packet filter cannot see.
PerSourcePenalties yes
PerSourceMaxStartups 2
PerSourceNetBlockSize 32:128
